Software stack
The cleanest stack is Python on the Pi for motion control and telemetry, with React for the dashboard; Node is useful for frontend tooling, but the motion loop should stay in Python. Sensor-to-dashboard streaming over WebSockets is a proven Raspberry Pi pattern, and React WebSocket clients typically use reconnect, heartbeat, and throttling for stable real-time control.

Use these services:

motiond in Python: inverse kinematics, homing, safety limits, step generation, path planning.

api in Python FastAPI: REST for presets/admin, WebSocket for live control.

ui in React: joystick, map view, telemetry, presets, logs, settings.

Optional node dev server: Vite/Next.js during development only.

